			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4495398">
									

<p>I agree on omitting extraneous data, but disagree on everything else heavily. If you're going to omit something that I'm used to seeing in an article, it better have an actual reason for it. Articles that omit descriptions or containment procedures are interesting to me because it makes it feel like there's something wrong- it's the hook. But if the explanation is &quot;I just didn't feel like doing it&quot;, then it makes me a little grumpy because it just makes it seem lazy and amateurish.</p>

