														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4495405">
									

<p>I mean, there's a debate here about whether or not stories should be judged in a vacuum or judged in the context of other stories that are adjacent to them, and I guess the answer falls somewhere in the middle. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">That said, ascribing laziness to a deliberate authorial choice seems more like a reader problem, especially with the context of Cimmerian being as prolific as he is.</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-707319-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-707319-1')">1</a></sup></p>
<p>As we all know, the 5K Con just ended, and we got a lot of entries. Out of curiosity, have you read <a href="/scp-5790">SCP-5790</a>? Same principle, really; why explain what the anomaly was, even in the abstract of &quot;it was something that needed to be forgotten&quot;, when you could just expunge it?</p>
